<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3183] ScanQuery and localEntries are ignored keepBinary flag in OFFHEAP_TIERED mode</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3183</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;ScanQuery&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;localEntries&lt;/tt&gt; method returns iterator which contains deserialized entries but they have been called with withKeepBinary flag. Reproducible test attached.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12972054">IGNITE-3183</key>
            <summary>ScanQuery and localEntries are ignored keepBinary flag in OFFHEAP_TIERED mode</summary>
                <type id="1" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&amp;avatarId=21133&amp;avatarType=issuetype">Bug</type>
                                            <priority id="3" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/priorities/major.svg">Major</priority>
                        <status id="6" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/statuses/closed.png" description="The issue is considered finished, the resolution is correct. Issues which are not closed can be reopened.">Closed</status>
                    <statusCategory id="3" key="done" colorName="green"/>
                                    <resolution id="1">Fixed</resolution>
                                        <assignee username="avinogradov">Anton Vinogradov (Obsolete, actual is &quot;av&quot;)</assignee>
                                    <reporter username="ntikhonov">Nikolay Tikhonov</reporter>
                        <labels>
                            <label>important</label>
                    </labels>
                <created>Mon, 23 May 2016 13:11:45 +0000</created>
                <updated>Wed, 10 May 2017 08:15:52 +0000</updated>
                            <resolved>Thu, 2 Jun 2016 14:08:14 +0000</resolved>
                                    <version>1.6</version>
                                    <fixVersion>1.7</fixVersion>
                                    <component>cache</component>
                        <due></due>
                            <votes>0</votes>
                                    <watches>4</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="15297712" author="dmagda" created="Tue, 24 May 2016 05:31:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The issue is only related to keys. Everything works fine for values. If not to use custom objects as the keys then the tests would pass.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15298023" author="ntikhonov" created="Tue, 24 May 2016 10:06:04 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;In case &lt;tt&gt;localEntries&lt;/tt&gt; the issue is releted to values and keys.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15299547" author="ntikhonov" created="Wed, 25 May 2016 06:35:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Anton, &lt;br/&gt;
Could you please improve attached test? Would be greate if you add more variation of cache configuration (with swap, store and etc). &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15299656" author="sboikov" created="Wed, 25 May 2016 08:11:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Anton,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Please also add tests for these cases:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;localEntries when there are entries in near cache&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;localEntries with different CachePeekMode&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;use &apos;keepBinary&apos; but key/values are primitive types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="15301951" author="avinogradov" created="Thu, 26 May 2016 11:12:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Proposals implemented, please review.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15303945" author="sboikov" created="Fri, 27 May 2016 11:16:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Reviewed, I didn&apos;t like that method &apos;context.keepBinary&apos; which is based on thread-local variable is called from random places, I changed this to call it once in GridCacheAdapter and pass to all &apos;terators&apos; methods, please take a look at my changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also it isn&apos;t clear why key and value are handled differently in &apos;GridCacheQueryManager.scanIterator&apos;, could you please explain this?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15304108" author="avinogradov" created="Fri, 27 May 2016 14:18:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Semen,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That&apos;s behavior was not changed. &lt;br/&gt;
Previously object deserialised at AbstractLazySwapEntry.key() ignoring keepBinary flag.&lt;br/&gt;
Now it deserialised at org/apache/ignite/internal/processors/cache/query/GridCacheQueryManager.java:1160&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                    </comments>
